SOAPBOX: This was another last minute QRP operation from the
SOAPBOX: WA6TQT Superstation in Anza.
SOAPBOX: Having access to stacked arrays made up for running only 5-watts.
SOAPBOX: The problem was people jumping on my run frequencies w/o asking QRL first.
SOAPBOX: I pick ODDBALL run frequencies, so if you are calling CQ on top of me,
SOAPBOX: that is NO accident.
SOAPBOX: My QRP signal busted many HUGE pileups caused by people not following
SOAPBOX: the operators instructions. When he asks "WQ6?" and you send your KB6LID
SOAPBOX: callsign on top of me, then you waste everybody's time.
SOAPBOX: So, when the pandemonium subsides I slip the WQ6X call in ONCE,
SOAPBOX: make the QSO and exit the morass of poor operating ethics - leaving them to
SOAPBOX: fight it out amongst their chaotically-created MESS.
SOAPBOX: The variety of CooL countries on the air this weekend was AMAZING.
SOAPBOX: Altho noisy space-WX, the propagation was quite nice - despite weaker
SOAPBOX: signals from central Europe. The K3/0-mini picked them up nicely, except
SOAPBOX: when the RX front-end would overload (preamp off) and the AGC would drop the
SOAPBOX: RX gain. I thought the K3 was supposed to have the BEST Dynamic Range - guess
SOAPBOX: knot.
SOAPBOX: LooK for a write-up on this at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
